 "transcript": [
  "[action] goes to see father",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"I should have been made an officer long ago and not my brother. He is still only a son and yet he is already setting up a great market, and I, your eldest son, have been made a mere officer among the rich men.\"",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung listens to his eldest son's complaints.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"I will not be content, and if I am not given what is due to me I will leave and go away and live with another wife and a house of my own and let the men and the women in my own house decide how they shall live.\"",
  "[silence] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung says nothing.",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) goes to eldest son's court",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung sits on the court steps and smokes his pipe.",
  "[action] (to the second son) Eldest son watches his brother's market.",
  "[action] Wang Lung goes to the market.",
  "[action] Wang Lung buys rice from his second son.",
  "[action] Wang Lung eats rice at night.",
  "[action] Wang Lung sleeps and dreams.",
  "[action] Wang Lung sleeps and hears a woman.",
  "[action] Wang Lung goes to the kitchen.",
  "[action] (to the second son) Eldest son goes to second son's court.",
  "[action] Wang Lung sleeps and wakes.",
  "[action] Eldest son visits second son's court.",
  "the second son (to the eldest son): \"It is a good thing to have a son who can see into the future,\"",
  "the second son (to the eldest son): \"and it is not every man who can see the good in a road when others see only a road.\"",
  "[action] The second son laughs and looks at his brother."
 ],
